  "title": "The \"Podcast\" ECoG dataset",
  "description": "The \"Podcast\" ECoG dataset contains intracranial electrocorticography recordings from 9 participants (1,330 grid, depth, and strip electrodes) who listened to a 30-minute naturalistic story containing over 5,000 words. It provides raw data, a minimally preprocessed high-gamma version, the auditory stimulus, an aligned word-level transcript, and linguistic features ranging from acoustic properties to large language model embeddings. Tutorials replicating earlier findings are included to support research on natural language comprehension.",
  "methods_description": "Participants undergoing intracranial monitoring listened to a 30-minute spoken story while ECoG was recorded from grid, depth, and strip electrodes. A minimally preprocessed high-gamma band version is provided, along with word-level transcripts aligned to the audio and linguistic features including LLM embeddings.",
